      "description": "The Sri Prasanna Anjaneya Gudi is a small temple dedicated to Lord Hanuman, located on Hemakuta Hill in Hampi, and reflects the traditional architectural style of the Vijayanagara Empire. Measuring approximately 8 feet by 8 feet, the temple is accompanied by a stunning Plumeria ( Plumeria ) tree that grows on the same pedestal, enhancing the site's beauty and serenity. This charming structure, surrounded by the natural splendor of the hill, stands as a testament to Hampi's rich cultural heritage and the enduring devotion to Lord Hanuman.",
